​"The 'Death Machine'

​A 'little' commission job with only two specific requirements:

1. ​Auto all the time.
  This is achievable in software, but we physically bridged the selector switch to suit the customer's requirements.

2. ​Realistic cyclic rate.
  Setting it to 11 gave it a magic sound.

​The engine was a little loose, so a custom 3D-printed shim was made to hold it firm. We wired the original trigger switch to the Polarstar trigger board, adding a solid layer of glue to support the wires at the board.

​The barrel they had installed previously appeared not to be finished after cutting, so it went on the lathe and a clean little bevel finished the job.
